  "solutionMarkdown": "The $n^{th}$ term of an arithmetic progression is given by $a_n = a + (n-1)d$. Here, $a=5$, $d=3$, and we are looking for the fifth term ($n=5$). Substituting these values in: \n\n$$a_5 = 5 + (5-1) \\cdot 3 = 5 + 4\\cdot 3 = 5 + 12 = 17.$$",
